 to=self<|message|>Write an story about the school life of a teenage student who is secretly a wood elf.

We need story. Probably first person? Teenage student secretly wood elf. School life. Provide stylistic issues? User is high school student from Hong Kong, native language not English, occasionally stylistic issues and grammar mistakes. The prompt says you are helpful... The user asks write story. Should we mimic their style? Probably write story in good English. Probably just write story.

Make it engaging. Secretly wood elf. School life.

Let's produce story with some subtlety.<|start|>assistant to=user<|message|>My name is Lin. I am 16 years old. I go to St. Francis Secondary School in Kowloon. I am in Form 4. Everyone thinks I am just a quiet girl who is always late because of the bus.

The truth is I am not late. I am slow.

I am a wood elf.

My mother brought me to Hong Kong when I was 7, after the forest in the north was cut down. She said we must hide. Humans do not like elves. They think we are stories. So we live in a small flat in Sham Shui Po, and I go to school like a normal student.

School life is hard for me.

First, the uniform. The white shirt and navy skirt is itchy. My skin is used to bark and moss. I have to wear socks every day. My feet are used to be bare on the ground. I can feel the earth through the floor in the classroom, but the socks make it quiet. I hate it.

Second, the smell. Canteen smells like fried pork chop and soy sauce. It is good, but it is too strong. I can smell the plastic lunch boxes and the cleaning liquid in the toilet. My nose is too good. In the forest, I can smell rain coming three days before. Here, I can smell my classmate, Mei, eating garlic bread from the morning. I want to tell her to brush her teeth.

Third, the noise. The bell is very loud. It hurts my ears. The students shout in the corridor. The air conditioner hums all day. At home in the forest, the loudest sound was birds and wind. Here, the teacher uses a microphone. I have to cover my ears with my hair.

But I like some things.

I like biology class. When Miss Chan talks about photosynthesis, I want to raise my hand and say, "Yes, but the trees also listen." I don't. I just write notes.

I like the school garden behind the building. It is small, only three meters by five meters, with some tomato plants and a broken bench. No one goes there at lunch. I go there. I sit on the ground and take off my socks. I put my hands on the soil. It is dry and hot from the sun, but it is real earth. I can feel it. For five minutes, I am not Lin the student. I am Lin the elf. I can hear the small insects. I can smell the real soil under the concrete.

Last week, my friend, Alex, found me there. He is the boy who always sits next to me in math. He saw me with no socks and my ears... I have pointy ears. I always wear my hair down to hide them. But the wind blew my hair.

He did not run away. He just said, "Your ears are cool. Are you a fairy?"

I was scared. I said, "No. It's just hair."

He smiled and said, "Okay. Can I sit with you? The garden is nice."

Now he comes with me every day at lunch. He brings two apples. He does not ask questions. He just sits quietly. Sometimes he reads his book. Sometimes he just looks at the tomato plants.

I think maybe I can be both. I can be a student with homework and exams, and I can be an elf who loves the earth. I just need to hide my ears better, and maybe wear softer socks.

Tomorrow is the school sports day. I have to run 100 meters. My legs are fast, like a deer. I will try not to win too much. [end of text]


